--- stderr ---
error: a bracket pair parameter cannot be a block pattern
  ┌─ tests/harness/errors/383_bracket_pair_monad_marker_content.eu:3:2
  │
3 │ ⟦{x}⟧: { :monad bind(m, f): f(m)  return(a): a }
  │  ^^^
  │
  = a bracket pair always receives its items as a list, so its parameter is a name (`⟦ xs ⟧`) or a list pattern (`⟦ [x, y] ⟧`)
  = to destructure a single block item, put the block pattern in a list pattern: `⟦ [{m}] ⟧: m`
  = an empty block `⟦{}⟧: { :monad … }` declares a monadic bracket pair
